---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Amido';
const description =
  'How Amido handles website, app, account, diary, AI, support and billing data.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
      <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <header class="mb-10">
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
            This policy covers the Amido website, the Amido applications, your Amido account and
            diary, AI meal analysis, support messages, and subscriptions.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">1. Controller and contact</h2>
          <address class="not-italic bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6">
            <strong class="text-gray-900">Emanuele Viglianisi</strong><br />
            Altenbauerstraße 12<br />
            4060 Leonding, Austria<br />
            <a href="mailto:emavgl.app@gmail.com" class="text-brand hover:underline">emavgl.app@gmail.com</a>
          </address>
          <p>No data protection officer has been appointed. Privacy questions and requests can be sent to the address or email above.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">2. The website</h2>
          <p>Amido does not operate advertising, profiling or third-party analytics on this website, and does not set non-essential cookies.</p>
          <p>When you visit, the hosting and content-delivery infrastructure may process technical request data such as your IP address, date and time, requested URL, referrer, browser and device information, response status, and security events. The purpose is to deliver the site, protect it against abuse, and keep it secure and available. The legal basis is the legitimate interest in operating a secure public service (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">3. The Amido application</h2>
          <p>Amido is an AI food logger. It processes the meals you describe, photograph or scan to estimate ingredients and nutrition. Your diary — meal descriptions, ingredients, quantities, nutrition values and dates — is stored <strong class="text-gray-900">only on your device</strong>, not on our servers. Your profile and preferences (language, appearance and theme, text size, tracked facts, meal tips, opening screen and any Nightscout configuration) are stored on your device as well.</p>
          <p>Using the app requires signing in with Google or Apple. The account is used for the AI service, fair-use limits and subscriptions — not to store your diary. There is no cross-device sync. You can export a backup file and import it on another device or after reinstalling (see below).</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">4. Accounts and diary data</h2>
          <p><strong class="text-gray-900">Account.</strong> Amido uses social sign-in only (Google or Apple). We receive the email address and account identifier from the provider and store an internal user id, a display username, the account creation date and — if you subscribe — a subscription status and a payment-provider customer reference. We do not receive or store passwords. Your sign-in token is stored on your device.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-gray-900">Diary.</strong> Your diary is stored on your device. We do not receive the meal descriptions, ingredients, quantities, nutrition values or timestamps you save, except when you actively submit a meal for AI analysis (see the next section) or contact support. Deleting the app, or using “Delete diary on this device” in Settings → Your data, removes it. There is no server-side diary and no cross-device sync.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-gray-900">Fair use.</strong> The server keeps a daily counter of AI requests per account to enforce the fair-use limit. It contains no meal content.</p>
          <p><strong class="text-gray-900">Device backups and exports.</strong> If you enable iCloud Backup (iOS) or device backup (Android), the operating system may include the diary in its backup. That backup is controlled by Apple or Google and is not accessible to us. You can export a portable JSON backup at any time in Settings → Your data, and import it later. The legal basis is the performance of the service you requested (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR) and, where relevant, your consent.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">5. AI analysis and food databases</h2>
          <p>When you describe a meal or submit a photo, the text and/or image is sent to third-party artificial-intelligence providers to extract ingredients, quantities and nutrition estimates. That content is processed to generate your result and is subject to those providers' terms and privacy policies. We may keep a meal description in operational diagnostic logs to debug extraction; those logs are request-scoped and are not linked to your account (no username, email or user id is written with them). Do not submit information you are not comfortable sharing with those providers.</p>
          <p>Nutrient values are then looked up in public food-composition databases (for example Open Food Facts, USDA and the Canadian Nutrient File) and, where enabled, a decision model is used to pick the most suitable database entry. Results are estimates and may be inaccurate or incomplete — always verify them.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">6. Nightscout (optional, device-only)</h2>
          <p>If you enable Nightscout, Amido writes the meals you log to your own Nightscout site directly from your device. Your Nightscout URL and token are stored on your device and are never sent to Amido's servers. Whether and how Nightscout processes that data is governed by your own Nightscout setup.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">7. Subscriptions and payments</h2>
          <p>Subscriptions are purchased through the Apple App Store or Google Play in the mobile apps, and through Stripe on the web. Purchases are processed by those providers under their own terms and privacy policies. Amido receives only the information needed to determine whether your subscription is active, such as a customer or purchase reference and its status. Amido does <strong class="text-gray-900">not</strong> receive or store your payment card details.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">8. Support messages</h2>
          <p>If you contact Amido, the email address, message, attachments, technical headers and any information you include are processed to answer your request, handle bug reports, and protect legal interests. The legal basis is taking steps at your request and the legitimate interest in support and service security (Article 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR). Support correspondence is kept only as long as needed to resolve the request and, where applicable, to meet legal record-keeping or limitation periods. Public GitHub issues are processed by GitHub under GitHub's policies.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">9. Recipients and international transfers</h2>
          <p>Depending on how you use Amido, recipients may include the identity providers used for sign-in (Google or Apple), the hosting and content-delivery providers that run the website and server, the AI providers that analyse meals and the public food databases consulted, the payment provider for subscriptions, and the email providers used to exchange support messages. Some of these services may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where that happens, transfers rely on the safeguards described by the relevant provider, such as an adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">10. Your rights</h2>
          <p>Subject to the applicable legal conditions, you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, or data portability, and you may object to processing based on legitimate interests. Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time; this does not affect processing carried out before withdrawal.</p>
          <p>You can export a copy of your diary and delete the on-device copy at any time in Settings → Your data. Deleting your account removes the account, usage counters and subscription data from our servers.</p>
          <p>You can exercise these rights by contacting the controller above. You also have the right to complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand hover:underline">Datenschutzbehörde</a>, Barichgasse 40-42, 1030 Vienna, <a href="mailto:dsb@dsb.gv.at" class="text-brand hover:underline">dsb@dsb.gv.at</a>).</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">11. Retention and required data</h2>
          <p>Account data is kept for as long as your account exists. Deleting your account removes the account, usage counters and subscription data from our servers. Your diary is not stored on our servers; it remains on your device until you delete it in Settings → Your data or uninstall the app. Diagnostic logs (including anonymous meal descriptions) are used only for debugging and are not linked to your account. Device backups may retain a copy according to Apple's or Google's retention rules.</p>
          <p>Providing personal data is generally voluntary. Without technical request data the website cannot be delivered; without an account the AI features cannot be provided; and without payment-provider processing a subscription cannot be completed or restored.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">12. Changes</h2>
          <p>This policy may be updated when the website, applications, providers or legal requirements change. The current version is always published on this page.</p>
        </section>

        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">Last updated: 26 October 2026</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
